cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
title: "mars-earth: A Pure Python Implementation of Multivariate Adaptive Regression Splines"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Mordaunt
    given-names: Dylan A.
  - family-names: Schuler
    given-names: Alejandro
abstract: >
  mars-earth is a pure Python implementation of Multivariate Adaptive
  Regression Splines (MARS), providing a scikit-learn compatible API without
  C/Cython dependencies. The Python import namespace remains pymars for
  compatibility with existing code. Version 2 is a rewrite of the fitting
  code in the fork alejandroschuler/mars, checked against the R package earth.
repository-code: "https://github.com/alejandroschuler/mars"
url: "https://github.com/alejandroschuler/mars"
version: 2.0.0.dev0
license: Apache-2.0
keywords:
  - "mars-earth"
  - "mars"
  - "pymars"
  - "multivariate adaptive regression splines"
  - "machine learning"
  - "scikit-learn"
  - "python"
  - "regression"
  - "classification"
